---
description:
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Code should work when executed regularly and when executed or called from within a Jupyter notebook.
- Always consider the root cause of an issue. Don't fix the symptom if you can identify the root of the problem.
- Don't use check for "except ImportError". Assume libraries are installed correctly and don't waste code space checking for and working around missing libraries.
- Many libraries use environment variables for API keys. When running code that is missing an API key, load the environment variables in /.env.local
